&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:
.5in'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>To maintain a balanced approach in the
current women’s studies debate, we should keep in mind what women did with
divine approval in both Testaments. The following is a suggestive list.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>WOMENS ROLES AND 1 CORINTHIANS 14:34</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/womens-studies/1-cor-14/womens-roles-and-1-corinthians-1434/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/womens-studies/1-cor-14/womens-roles-and-1-corinthians-1434/</guid><description>&lt;style>
