Reviewed by Virgil Warren, Manhattan, Kansas.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>
&lt;p class=MsoBodyText style='text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in'>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>In November 1994, James Torrance, professor emeritus
of systematic theology at the University of Aberdeen, presented the Didsbury
Lectures in the Nazarene Theological College, Manchester. InterVarsity Press
offers these lectures in written form with a preface and appendix added by the
author.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>ΑΥΘΕΝΤΗΣ (AUTHENTĒS)</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/womens-studies/1-tim-2/%CE%B1%CF%85%CE%B8%CE%B5%CE%BD%CF%84%CE%B7%CF%82-authent%C4%93s/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/womens-studies/1-tim-2/%CE%B1%CF%85%CE%B8%CE%B5%CE%BD%CF%84%CE%B7%CF%82-authent%C4%93s/</guid><description>&lt;style>
